---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
---

<GuideLayout
  title="Understanding Extraction Yield & TDS"
  description="What extraction yield means, how TDS works, and why these numbers are the key to consistently great coffee. A practical guide with formulas and examples."
  headline="Understanding Extraction Yield <em>& TDS</em>"
  subtitle="The science behind why some cups taste incredible and others don't — and the two numbers that explain the difference."
  heroAccent="science"
  readTime="8 min"
  category="Science"
>

<h2>The Problem Extraction Yield Solves</h2>

<p>
  You brew a perfect cup on Tuesday. On Wednesday, you try to repeat it — same beans, same method — and it's not as good. What changed? Without measurement, you're guessing. <strong>Extraction yield gives you a number that describes exactly how much flavour you pulled from your coffee.</strong>
</p>

<p>
  Think of coffee grounds like a sponge full of flavour compounds. Some of those compounds taste great (sugars, acids, aromatics). Some taste terrible (bitter tannins, astringent phenols). Extraction yield tells you what percentage of the solubles you actually dissolved into the water.
</p>

<div class="key-insight">
  <div class="ki-accent"></div>
  <div class="ki-body">
    <div class="ki-label">The Sweet Spot</div>
    <p>The SCA defines the ideal extraction yield range as <strong>18–22%</strong>. Below 18% you're under-extracting (sour, thin). Above 22% you're over-extracting (bitter, harsh). The magic happens in between.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Two Numbers That Tell You Everything</h2>

<div class="two-numbers">
  <div class="tn-card">
    <div class="tn-header">
      <span class="tn-abbr">TDS%</span>
      <span class="tn-full">Total Dissolved Solids</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tn-value">1.15 – 1.45%</div>
    <div class="tn-ideal">Ideal range for filter coffee</div>
    <p>TDS measures the <strong>concentration</strong> of your brew — how strong the cup is. It's the percentage of dissolved coffee solids in the liquid. You measure it with a refractometer.</p>
    <div class="tn-analogy">
      <strong>Analogy:</strong> If coffee is a glass of lemonade, TDS is how sweet or sour it tastes per sip.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="tn-card">
    <div class="tn-header">
      <span class="tn-abbr">EY%</span>
      <span class="tn-full">Extraction Yield</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tn-value">18 – 22%</div>
    <div class="tn-ideal">Ideal range for balanced flavour</div>
    <p>EY measures <strong>how much</strong> of the coffee you actually extracted. Out of all the solubles in your grounds, what percentage ended up in your cup? It's calculated from TDS, not measured directly.</p>
    <div class="tn-analogy">
      <strong>Analogy:</strong> If coffee is lemonade, EY is how much juice you squeezed from the lemons — regardless of how much water you added.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>The Formula</h2>

<p>Extraction yield is calculated, not measured. Here's the formula:</p>

<div class="formula-card">
  <div class="formula-main">
    EY% = (Brew Weight × TDS%) ÷ Dose × 100
  </div>
  <div class="formula-example">
    <div class="fe-label">Example</div>
    <div class="fe-grid">
      <div class="fe-item">
        <span class="fe-val">15 g</span>
        <span class="fe-key">Coffee dose</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fe-item">
        <span class="fe-val">240 g</span>
        <span class="fe-key">Brew weight (in cup)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fe-item">
        <span class="fe-val">1.35%</span>
        <span class="fe-key">TDS reading</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fe-calc">
      <span class="fe-calc-line">EY = (240 × 0.0135) ÷ 15 × 100</span>
      <span class="fe-calc-line">EY = 3.24 ÷ 15 × 100</span>
      <span class="fe-calc-result">EY = 21.6%</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fe-verdict">✓ Right in the sweet spot</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>What the Numbers Mean in Your Cup</h2>

<div class="extraction-zones">
  <div class="ez-zone ez-zone--under">
    <div class="ez-range">&lt; 18%</div>
    <h3>Under-Extracted</h3>
    <div class="ez-traits">
      <span>Sour</span>
      <span>Salty</span>
      <span>Thin</span>
      <span>Quick finish</span>
    </div>
    <p>Not enough flavour was pulled from the grounds. The pleasant sweet and bitter compounds are still locked inside. You're only getting the first wave — fast-dissolving acids.</p>
    <div class="ez-fix">
      <strong>Fix:</strong> Grind finer, brew longer, or increase temperature.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ez-zone ez-zone--ideal">
    <div class="ez-range">18 – 22%</div>
    <h3>Ideal Extraction</h3>
    <div class="ez-traits">
      <span>Sweet</span>
      <span>Complex</span>
      <span>Balanced</span>
      <span>Clean finish</span>
    </div>
    <p>The balance point. Enough acid for brightness, enough sugar for sweetness, just enough bitterness for depth. This is where coffee sings.</p>
    <div class="ez-fix ez-fix--good">
      <strong>Goal:</strong> Reproduce this consistently. Log your parameters.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ez-zone ez-zone--over">
    <div class="ez-range">&gt; 22%</div>
    <h3>Over-Extracted</h3>
    <div class="ez-traits">
      <span>Bitter</span>
      <span>Astringent</span>
      <span>Dry</span>
      <span>Hollow</span>
    </div>
    <p>Too much was pulled — including the harsh, late-dissolving compounds (tannins, phenols) that make coffee taste like you're chewing on a tea bag.</p>
    <div class="ez-fix">
      <strong>Fix:</strong> Grind coarser, brew shorter, or lower temperature.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Do You Actually Need a Refractometer?</h2>

<p>
  Refractometers (like the VST or Atago) cost $100–$700. <strong>You don't need one to brew great coffee.</strong> But if you're the type of person who loves data and wants to dial in objectively rather than by feel, it's a game-changer.
</p>

<p>
  Without a refractometer, you can still use extraction principles by:
</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Tasting deliberately.</strong> If it's sour, you're under-extracting. If it's bitter, you're over-extracting. Adjust one variable at a time.</li>
  <li><strong>Tracking brew parameters.</strong> Log dose, water, grind, time, and taste rating. Over time, you'll see which combinations consistently produce the best cups.</li>
  <li><strong>Using the Brewio calculator.</strong> The app's built-in extraction yield calculator lets you input TDS and dose and instantly see your EY% — no math required.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How Variables Affect Extraction</h2>

<p>Every brew variable pushes extraction in a direction. Here's your cheat sheet:</p>

<div class="variables-grid">
  <div class="var-card">
    <h3>Grind Size</h3>
    <div class="var-bar">
      <span class="var-end">Coarser</span>
      <div class="var-track"><div class="var-arrow">→</div></div>
      <span class="var-end">Finer</span>
    </div>
    <p>Finer grind = more surface area = faster and higher extraction. The single most impactful variable.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="var-card">
    <h3>Water Temperature</h3>
    <div class="var-bar">
      <span class="var-end">Cooler</span>
      <div class="var-track"><div class="var-arrow">→</div></div>
      <span class="var-end">Hotter</span>
    </div>
    <p>Hotter water extracts faster. 90–96°C is the standard range. Below 85°C, extraction drops significantly.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="var-card">
    <h3>Brew Time</h3>
    <div class="var-bar">
      <span class="var-end">Shorter</span>
      <div class="var-track"><div class="var-arrow">→</div></div>
      <span class="var-end">Longer</span>
    </div>
    <p>Longer contact time = more extraction. But after a point, you're only extracting the harsh compounds.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="var-card">
    <h3>Agitation</h3>
    <div class="var-bar">
      <span class="var-end">Less</span>
      <div class="var-track"><div class="var-arrow">→</div></div>
      <span class="var-end">More</span>
    </div>
    <p>Stirring and pouring agitation speed up extraction. A gentle swirl vs. aggressive stirring makes a noticeable difference.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="tip-callout">
  <div class="tip-icon">💡</div>
  <div>
    <strong>Change one variable at a time.</strong> If your coffee is sour and you simultaneously grind finer AND increase temperature, you won't know which change fixed it. This is the scientific method applied to coffee — control your variables, and your journal becomes your lab notebook.
  </div>
</div>


<aside class="tool-promo">
  <a href="/tools/extraction-yield-calculator/">
    <span class="tp-label">Calculate your extraction yield</span>
    <span class="tp-desc">Enter dose, beverage weight, and TDS% to see whether you hit the 18–22% sweet spot.</span>
  </a>
</aside>

</GuideLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Key Insight ── */
  .key-insight {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .ki-accent {
    width: 4px;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--amber), var(--brown));
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .ki-body { padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; }

  .ki-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--amber);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .ki-body p { margin: 0 !important; font-size: 0.95rem !important; }

  /* ── Two Numbers ── */
  .two-numbers {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .tn-card {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 1.75rem;
  }

  .tn-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .tn-abbr {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .tn-full {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .tn-value {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--text-dark);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .tn-ideal {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--text-light);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .tn-card p { font-size: 0.9rem !important; }

  .tn-analogy {
    background: var(--cream-subtle);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 0.875rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .tn-analogy strong { color: var(--text-dark); }

  /* ── Formula ── */
  .formula-card {
    background: var(--dark);
    border-radius: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .formula-main {
    padding: 2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--amber);
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-dark);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .formula-example { padding: 2rem; }

  .fe-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: rgba(250,247,242,0.4);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .fe-grid {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .fe-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.15rem; }

  .fe-val {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  .fe-key {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: rgba(250,247,242,0.35);
  }

  .fe-calc {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-dark);
  }

  .fe-calc-line {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: rgba(250,247,242,0.5);
  }

  .fe-calc-result {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--amber);
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .fe-verdict {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #4ade80;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ── Extraction Zones ── */
  .extraction-zones {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .ez-zone {
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    background: white;
  }

  .ez-range {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .ez-zone--under .ez-range { color: #f59e0b; }
  .ez-zone--ideal .ez-range { color: #16a34a; }
  .ez-zone--over .ez-range  { color: #dc2626; }

  .ez-zone h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-dark);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem !important;
  }

  .ez-traits {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .ez-traits span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    background: var(--cream-subtle);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 100px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .ez-zone p { font-size: 0.85rem !important; margin-bottom: 0.75rem !important; }

  .ez-fix {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-dark);
    background: var(--cream-subtle);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .ez-fix--good { background: rgba(22,163,74,0.06); }

  /* ── Variables Grid ── */
  .variables-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .var-card {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .var-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-dark);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem !important;
  }

  .var-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .var-end {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--text-light);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .var-track {
    flex: 1;
    height: 6px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--border-subtle), var(--amber), var(--brown));
    border-radius: 3px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding-right: 2px;
  }

  .var-arrow {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: white;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-shadow: 0 0 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
  }

  .var-card p { font-size: 0.85rem !important; margin: 0 !important; }

  /* ── Tip Callout ── */
  .tip-callout {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    background: rgba(196,123,48,0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(196,123,48,0.15);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .tip-icon { font-size: 1.25rem; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.1rem; }
  .tip-callout strong { color: var(--text-dark); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .two-numbers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .extraction-zones { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .variables-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .formula-main { font-size: 0.85rem; }
  }

  .tool-promo { margin: 2.5rem 0; }

  .tool-promo a {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem;
    background: rgba(196,123,48,0.07);
    border: 1px solid rgba(196,123,48,0.22);
    border-radius: 14px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s, background 0.2s;
  }

  .tool-promo a:hover { border-color: var(--amber); background: rgba(196,123,48,0.11); }
  .tool-promo a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--amber); outline-offset: 2px; }

  .tool-promo .tp-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .tool-promo .tp-desc { font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-muted); }
</style>
